===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[breathy]] sound like that of an object passing at high speed, or like the sound of air swiftly moving (such as from a leaking oxygen tank)
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2012|author=John Branch|title=Snow Fall: The Avalanche at Tunnel Creek|newspaper=The New York Times|url=http://www.nytimes.com/projects/2012/snow-fall/?smid=fb-nytimes&WT.z_sma=SP_SNT_20130415#/?part=tunnel-creek}}
#*: The snow burst through the trees with no warning but a last-second '''whoosh''' of sound, a two-story wall of white and Chris Rudolph’s piercing cry: “Avalanche! Elyse!”
#* "I love deadlines. I like the '''whooshing''' sound they make as they fly by." —Douglas Adams
* A [[swishy]] sound caused by two pieces of fabric (e.g. corduroy) rubbing against each other.

